::JOUR_U06_L02_QUIZ_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.REP.02] Source: Reporting Package Verification. Task: A reporter is preparing a package about after-school tutoring attendance. Claim: Attendance increased after peer tutors began visiting ninth-grade classes. Evidence Available: sign-in sheets from September and October, one interview with the tutoring coordinator, one student quote, and a hallway observation. Verification Concern: the sign-in sheets show more names in October, but the reporter has not checked whether the increase came from classroom visits or another cause. Publication Need: the reporter must explain what the evidence proves, what it does not prove, and what still needs verification. Question: Question 1: Which answer best applies the lesson standard to the embedded journalism source? {
